<w>
	<!-- ============================================================
	     ZONE GRID

	     These nodes exist for one reason: TEXT.

	     Every other rectangle this mod draws - the four lines round a
	     section and the header bar under its name - is a plain static, and those are made from the CONTAINER'S own xml
	     node, which is guaranteed to exist because the game built the
	     container from it. A static made that way takes a texture, a
	     size, a position and a colour, and that is all any of them need.

	     A caption is the exception. Text carries a FONT and a COLOUR,
	     and both of those live in the xml rather than in the script - so
	     one node per section, because the captions are not one colour.

	     TWO SECTIONS, ONE AT A TIME. The backpack's, and the pockets'
	     for when no backpack is on. Only one of them is ever on screen.

	     letterica16 is the font the inventory itself uses for nearly
	     everything; "small" is not a font this game has, whatever it
	     appears to do.

	     The colours are the player's - "pockets milkysh pink ...
	     backpack dark green" - lifted a little from the values the
	     borders use, because a caption has to read on a dark bar
	     and a border only has to be seen.

	     The numbers are placeholders. The draw pass overwrites position
	     and size every frame from the player's own cell size, so the
	     inventory can be set to any scale and the header still lands on
	     the section it belongs to. What matters is that each node
	     EXISTS: InitTextWnd on a path this file does not declare is a
	     hard failure in game, and the draw runs inside a pcall, so the
	     symptom would be a header that silently never appears.
	     ============================================================ -->
	<grid>
		<hdr x="0" y="0" width="100" height="16">
			<text align="c" vert_align="c" font="letterica16"
			      r="230" g="230" b="230" a="255"/>
		</hdr>
		<hdr_pouches x="0" y="0" width="100" height="16">
			<text align="c" vert_align="c" font="letterica16"
			      r="240" g="212" b="219" a="255"/>
		</hdr_pouches>
		<hdr_backpack x="0" y="0" width="100" height="16">
			<text align="c" vert_align="c" font="letterica16"
			      r="142" g="198" b="147" a="255"/>
		</hdr_backpack>
	</grid>
</w>
